<h1>John Kelly</h1>
<p>Lobbyist and security company founder. Candidate for mayor of Chicago, on the ballot February 23, 2027.</p>
<p>Runs the lobbying firm All-Circo, whose clients include Bally&#39;s casino, and co-founded Sentinel Security; 53, from a four-generation Chicago family, married to the commentator Julie Kelly with two adult daughters. Filed on the first day; NBC has raised questions about a suburban home he calls a summer house.</p>
<p><a href="/directdemocracy/app/candidate/tNryhx8sZkX1HFkBZmOCdkCte9F2">Full platform, open to comments</a></p>
<p><a href="https://johnkellyforchi.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign website (johnkellyforchi.com)</a></p>
<h2>What sets them apart</h2>
<p>Only Kelly: A city charter, a written constitution for city government. Kelly says Chicago is the only one of the 15 largest US cities without one.</p>
<p>Taxes: No new taxes of any kind, starting with property taxes. Johnson and Giannoulias want the wealthy to pay more; Nee will not rule out an increase.</p>
<p>Schools: Says CPS spends about 75 percent above the national average per student and should be judged on reading and math.</p>
<p>First cut: Names the mayor&#39;s 154-person security detail as the place to start.</p>
<h2>Where they split from the field</h2>
<p>Property taxes: Freeze or lower them, with Holberg and Kitover. Hold the city&#39;s levy flat: Giannoulias. An increase is not off the table: Nee.</p>
<p>New taxes: No new taxes, with Kitover. Make the wealthy pay more: Johnson and Giannoulias. Cut taxes: Wilson. Only as a last resort: Quigley.</p>
<h2>In their words</h2>
<ul>
<li>Give Chicago a city charter, a written constitution for city government. <q>A new City Charter changes who government works for.</q> (<a href="https://johnkellyforchi.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign platform (johnkellyforchi.com)</a>)</li>
<li>No new taxes of any kind, starting with property taxes. <q>you are able to bring property taxes down, and at least, at the very least, stabilize them,</q> (<a href="https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news/lobbyist-mayoral-candidate-john-kelly-chicago-career-politicians/" rel="nofollow noopener">CBS Chicago, Aug. 12, 2026</a>)</li>
<li>Judge the public schools on whether students can read and do math. <q>Teachers in Chicago’s classrooms work hard every day. They are not the problem.</q> (<a href="https://johnkellyforchi.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign platform (johnkellyforchi.com)</a>)</li>
<li>Start the cuts with the mayor&#39;s 154-person security detail. <q>you can cut 20 of those and buy five ambulances</q> (<a href="https://chicago.suntimes.com/fran-spielman-show/2026/08/20/chicago-mayoral-candidate-john-kelly-lobbyist-brandon-johnson-february-2027-election" rel="nofollow noopener">Sun-Times, Aug. 20, 2026, on the mayor&#39;s security detail</a>)</li>
</ul>
<h2>Campaign money</h2>
<ul>
<li>Committee: Citizens for John Kelly</li>
<li>Raised: $1.5M</li>
<li>Spent: $1.4M</li>
<li>Cash on hand: $2.5M</li>
<li>Raised July 1 to Sept. 30, 2026; spent Jan. 1 to Sept. 30, 2026. $1 million of the third quarter&#39;s money was loans from two companies, one of them his own security firm; the committee owes $1.25 million. <a href="https://elections.il.gov/CampaignDisclosure/CommitteeDetail.aspx?id=40942" rel="nofollow noopener">Source</a></li>
</ul>
<p>Money figures are each committee&#39;s quarterly reports to the Illinois State Board of Elections: spent is total expenditures from January 1 to September 30, 2026 (or since the committee formed), cash is funds available on September 30.</p>
<h2>Support</h2>
<p>Not listed in the ChicagoSpeaks poll, Sept. 2026 (Mansueto Institute / NORC). 0.0 points of support per $1 million spent.</p>
<h2>On money</h2>
<p>Would bring property taxes down or at least stabilize them, judge every expense by whether it is a good deal for taxpayers, and start the cuts with the mayor&#39;s security detail.</p>
<ul>
<li><q>Is this a good deal for the taxpayers?</q> (<a href="https://chicago.suntimes.com/fran-spielman-show/2026/08/20/chicago-mayoral-candidate-john-kelly-lobbyist-brandon-johnson-february-2027-election" rel="nofollow noopener">Sun-Times, Aug. 20, 2026, his stated guiding question</a>)</li>
<li><q>you can cut 20 of those and buy five ambulances</q> (<a href="https://chicago.suntimes.com/fran-spielman-show/2026/08/20/chicago-mayoral-candidate-john-kelly-lobbyist-brandon-johnson-february-2027-election" rel="nofollow noopener">Sun-Times, Aug. 20, 2026, on the mayor&#39;s security detail</a>)</li>
<li><q>you are able to bring property taxes down, and at least, at the very least, stabilize them,</q> (<a href="https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news/lobbyist-mayoral-candidate-john-kelly-chicago-career-politicians/" rel="nofollow noopener">CBS Chicago, Aug. 12, 2026</a>)</li>
</ul>
<h2>Pizza</h2>
<p>No position on record.</p>
